## STEP 1 — DELTA
- [CHANGED] Verified-ID mint premise refuted: `api.myaccount.microsoft.com` SPA source map shows `POST /api/issueVerifiedEmployeeCredential` sent with **empty body** (fetch POST, no `body`, no claim fields) → credential claims derive from the Bearer token identity, NOT client-supplied; prior "caller-chosen claims" reasoning in [75] is wrong.
- [NEW] `api.myaccount.microsoft.com` uniform token-gate: ALL paths incl. `/api/nonexistent-zzz` → 401 empty-body; NO anonymous branch, NO 404 differential (contrast api.mysignins which 404s unknown paths) — routing-policy only, not exploitable.
- [CHANGED] Accepted Graph 405 anomaly extends to `/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations` HEAD → 405 (len 0), same class.
- [NEW] `POST /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations` blank body → 401 `"Access token is empty"` (auth-gate-first; `$count=true` same 401) → no pre-auth schema leak; sharpens AUTH_HELPED steps (real Bearer mandatory).
- [NEW] No OpenAPI docs on either identity backend (`/swagger/v1/swagger.json` → mysignins 404, myaccount 401).

